WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.789 --> 00:00:05.150
In 1984, little Bastian Bux watched as the
unforgettable heroes from The NeverEnding

00:00:05.150 --> 00:00:08.320
Story battled against the Nothing to save
a kingdom from certain doom.

00:00:08.320 --> 00:00:12.150
The fantasy family film still resonates, but
what's become of its actors?

00:00:12.150 --> 00:00:15.610
Here's what the cast of The NeverEnding Story
looks like today.

00:00:15.610 --> 00:00:16.610
Barret Oliver

00:00:16.610 --> 00:00:20.680
Former child star Barrett Oliver got his big
Hollywood break by playing our heroic reader

00:00:20.680 --> 00:00:22.970
Bastian Bux in The NeverEnding Story.

00:00:22.970 --> 00:00:24.360
"It's only a story!

00:00:24.360 --> 00:00:25.400
It's not real!

00:00:25.400 --> 00:00:28.090
It's only a story!"

00:00:28.090 --> 00:00:32.810
He went on to claim starring roles in Tim
Burton's 1984 short film Frankenweenie, 1985's

00:00:32.810 --> 00:00:36.520
family sci-fi film D.A.R.Y.L., and Ron Howard's
Cocoon.

00:00:36.520 --> 00:00:38.860
In 1985, Oliver told Starlog,

00:00:38.860 --> 00:00:41.510
"I don't regret that I decided to become an
actor.

00:00:41.510 --> 00:00:44.450
Besides, if I don't like it at any time, I
can stop."

00:00:44.450 --> 00:00:46.490
And in 1989, he did just that.

00:00:46.490 --> 00:00:50.900
Oliver is now a photographic historian who
literally wrote the book on the Woodburytype

00:00:50.900 --> 00:00:52.970
printing process of the 19th century.

00:00:52.970 --> 00:00:57.060
He briefly returned to the front of the camera
in 2007, when he starred in a short documentary

00:00:57.060 --> 00:00:59.829
about his craft, called "In the Usual Manner."

00:00:59.829 --> 00:01:01.270
Noah Hathaway

00:01:01.270 --> 00:01:04.940
Atreyu was something of a comeback kid in
The NeverEnding Story — he endured the depressing

00:01:04.940 --> 00:01:09.390
death of his horse and still managed to battle
back existential forces of destruction.

00:01:09.390 --> 00:01:13.390
His real-life counterpart, Noah Hathaway,
seems to share that resilience: the actor

00:01:13.390 --> 00:01:16.960
has returned to Hollywood after nearly 20
years away from the spotlight.

00:01:16.960 --> 00:01:21.780
Before The NeverEnding Story, Hathaway's credits
included 1978's Battlestar Galactica, as well

00:01:21.780 --> 00:01:27.170
as appearances on many popular shows like
Mork &amp; Mindy, CHiPs, and Laverne &amp; Shirley.

00:01:27.170 --> 00:01:31.320
He quit the business after starring in 1986's
Troll because, as he told The News Tribune,

00:01:31.320 --> 00:01:35.780
he "just wanted to drop off the radar and
be a regular human being" for a while.

00:01:35.780 --> 00:01:39.541
After his career as a child star, Hathaway
worked in finance and tattoo artistry, and

00:01:39.541 --> 00:01:44.260
decided to return to showbusiness in 2012
when he landed a role in Sushi Girl and began

00:01:44.260 --> 00:01:45.990
writing his own screenplays.

00:01:45.990 --> 00:01:47.689
Tami Stronach

00:01:47.689 --> 00:01:51.799
The Childlike Empress had no screen experience
to speak of when she nabbed the iconic role

00:01:51.799 --> 00:01:53.119
in The NeverEnding Story.

00:01:53.119 --> 00:01:56.710
Tami Stronach explained to Slashfilm that
she was accidentally spotted by a casting

00:01:56.710 --> 00:01:58.650
agent who arrived for lunch early.

00:01:58.650 --> 00:02:02.710
Stronach almost completely disappeared from
the screen to focus on professional dancing,

00:02:02.710 --> 00:02:07.380
which she employed in a 2008 foreign language
TV musical where she played a dancing doll.

00:02:07.380 --> 00:02:11.400
Now she runs her own company in New York,
and her decision to pursue a mostly non-Hollywood

00:02:11.400 --> 00:02:13.069
life was intentional, saying,

00:02:13.069 --> 00:02:18.019
"I love dancing and acting equally, and when
we were thrown a lot of these odd scripts,

00:02:18.019 --> 00:02:20.659
we just looked at each other and said, 'We're
not going to play this game right.'

00:02:20.659 --> 00:02:24.489
I made a decision that I would throw myself
into dance and that if I really missed acting,

00:02:24.489 --> 00:02:26.329
I would return to it as an adult...

00:02:26.329 --> 00:02:30.110
So that's what I did and I ended up dancing
for 20 years professionally in New York."

00:02:30.110 --> 00:02:34.430
She did end up frequenting the stage for several
years and helped develop the Paper Canoe Theater

00:02:34.430 --> 00:02:37.650
Company, once she started to miss the acting
business.

00:02:37.650 --> 00:02:38.849
Deep Roy

00:02:38.849 --> 00:02:42.749
The actor who played Teeny Weeny has had a
long and fruitful career in show business.

00:02:42.749 --> 00:02:46.819
The Kenya-born Deep Roy might actually be
better known for his parts in other TV and

00:02:46.819 --> 00:02:51.599
film roles, like Mr. Sin in Doctor Who, Mr.
Soggybottom in Big Fish, the Oompa Loompas

00:02:51.599 --> 00:02:55.659
in Tim Burton's Charlie and the Chocolate
Factory, or Keenser in the Star Trek films.

00:02:55.680 --> 00:02:56.760
"Achoo!"

00:02:57.889 --> 00:03:01.849
Although Roy was almost a decade into his
career before he starred in The NeverEnding

00:03:01.849 --> 00:03:04.849
Story, it was one of his first big film roles.

00:03:04.849 --> 00:03:09.879
He's pretty much been acting consistently
since 1976, and unlike his co-stars, he shows

00:03:09.879 --> 00:03:11.709
no signs of stopping.

00:03:11.709 --> 00:03:13.139
Tilo Prückner

00:03:13.139 --> 00:03:18.010
German actor Tilo Prückner would hardly be
recognizable to those who saw him in The NeverEnding

00:03:18.010 --> 00:03:21.980
Story, since so much makeup work went into
becoming his character, the Night Hob.

00:03:21.980 --> 00:03:26.249
However, Prückner has been acting in films
and television for decades and has over 200

00:03:26.249 --> 00:03:30.089
credits to his name, starting all the way
back in the late '60s.

00:03:30.089 --> 00:03:33.480
Most of his work has been in Europe — and
The NeverEnding Story was no exception, as

00:03:33.480 --> 00:03:37.769
it was filmed primarily in director Wolfgang
Petersen's native West Germany.

00:03:37.769 --> 00:03:39.109
Gerald McRaney

00:03:39.109 --> 00:03:43.359
The role of Bastian's dad in The NeverEnding
Story was brief, but actor Gerald McRaney

00:03:43.359 --> 00:03:46.980
has enjoyed a lot more screen time in his
subsequent projects.

00:03:46.980 --> 00:03:50.999
He'd developed a great small-screen résumé
before landing the small supporting role in

00:03:50.999 --> 00:03:54.340
the movie, and he's since continued to thrive
on television.

00:03:54.340 --> 00:03:58.260
Most notably, he starred in Simon &amp; Simon
for eight seasons before becoming the titular

00:03:58.260 --> 00:04:02.120
father character in the 1989 sitcom Major
Dad.

00:04:02.120 --> 00:04:07.150
He also enjoyed regular roles on Deadwood,
Jericho, House of Cards, and in 2016, appeared

00:04:07.150 --> 00:04:11.409
as a part of the ensemble cast of the NBC
drama This Is Us.

00:04:11.409 --> 00:04:12.409
Alan Oppenheimer

00:04:13.280 --> 00:04:16.419
"My little friends."

00:04:16.419 --> 00:04:20.370
The voice actor responsible for most of The
NeverEnding Story's most memorable non-human

00:04:20.370 --> 00:04:25.790
characters, including The Rockbiter, Falkor,
and G'mork, was Alan Oppenheimer, who's had

00:04:25.790 --> 00:04:28.900
an illustrious career in front of the mic
and the camera.

00:04:28.900 --> 00:04:33.320
His screen appearance credits include an Emmy-nominated
guest role on Murphy Brown, but his voice

00:04:33.320 --> 00:04:36.090
credits are practically...neverending.

00:04:36.090 --> 00:04:40.950
He's perhaps best known for his work on Filmation's
version of the Ghostbusters, and Transformers…

00:04:40.950 --> 00:04:41.990
"Yeeeaaaa.

00:04:41.990 --> 00:04:48.210
Alright knights let's go blam zingem!"

00:04:48.210 --> 00:04:50.520
...and He-Man and the Masters of the Universe.

00:04:50.520 --> 00:04:56.820
"Silence you fool, I've had it with your whining
and bumbling!"

00:04:56.820 --> 00:05:01.100
Even with all those amazing credits, he'll
always be ol' Falkor to us…

00:05:01.100 --> 00:05:03.480
"Wwwaaahhhhh!!"

